<title>USA: Pulitzer October revenues up 24.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Pulitzer October revenues up 24.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pulitzer Publishing Co said Wednesday revenues rose 24.7 percent for the five weeks ended November 3, climbing to $58.5 million from $46.9 million a year ago.</p>
<p>Year to date, revenues at the media company advanced 13.7 percent to $440.6 million from $387.6 million.</p>
<p>Results include revenues of Scripps League Newspapers Inc, which was acquired on July 1, 1996 and added $5.9 million to October's revenues and $23.0 million to year-to-date revenues.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
